plugin-hostd (0.13.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: 0.13.0 changelog lists the history, the planner, the LV2 latency
    and the CI savings
  * CI: give build and test 60 minutes
  * tests: make the two chain sabotage texts unique, and catch the two
    mutants no test noticed
  * fuzz: point the mutant citations at src/verbs.c and fuzz_command.c as the
    batch lays them out
  * release: plugin-hostd 0.13.0
  * sabotage: name the CLAP note-onset text by its closing parenthesis
  * fuzz: the chain mutant applies past the new plan handler
  * Answer plan, plan_get and plan_clear: gather the members, apply the
    segments as chains, keep the ones that did not change
  * Add the grouping planner as a pure function, and the reader of the cost
    in a qualification record
  * Declare plan, plan_get and plan_clear, the grouping reasons and the
    grouping settings
  * Bench: document the new modes and fields, run the unit tests in CI (#188)
  * Bench: table.sh renders the chains and grouping rows as markdown (#188)
  * Bench: plan and pool modes beside individual and chain (#188)
  * Bench: repeat each row and write the median with its spread (#188)
  * Bench: a fixed stress load, with and without it as two rows (#188)
  * Bench: count xruns and read the latency JACK reports (#188)
  * Bench schema: xruns, latency_frames, stress, repeats and spread; modes
    plan and pool (#188)
  * Probe runner: copy lv2_measure's latency and cost into the LV2 grid point
    (#200)
  * README: grouped workers against one process per plugin, measured
  * Expect history.json in the contract package's file list, and cite the
    design note by name
  * Count each worker's windows and deaths into the history; history_get and
    history_clear
  * Give the history summary as one word, and a save a full interval from the
    first tick
  * Read a worker's CPU time and Pss from /proc
  * Keep a running history of each plugin on this machine
  * Take the machine class from one place, src/machine.c
  * Move the directory and fsync helpers of the pin store into src/fsutil.c
  * ci: cancel superseded pull request runs, skip package and fuzz runs a
    pull request cannot change
  * Render the vocabulary with omx-contract 3.4.0 and raise the floor to it
  * Create state_root at start so an add does not answer -503 over a missing
    directory (#180)
  * Design note: no pointer into a private repository
  * Bench: stop a stray with SIGTERM before SIGKILL
  * Design note: tidy the L8 cell
  * Design note: name the lane issues
  * Design note: group plugins into the fewest workers from pins and running
    history (#182)
  * debian: the protocol clients of plugin-hostd-tests carry no execute bit
  * Bench: one example document, a real run of class ci
  * Bench: a plugin no LV2 bundle names is unsupported, not a failed add
  * CI: the tests package lists the two protocol clients it ships
  * plugin-hostd-tests ships one protocol client for shell and Python, and
    the harness uses it (#177)
  * Bench: how to run it and read it, and a CI job for the harness
  * Bench: break each guard and watch it go red
  * Bench: the runner and the scenario table
  * Bench: the omx-bench/1 schema and its validator
  * CI: add the channel with the add-openmixer action
  * Docs: add the repository by installing openmixer-release

